When a Principle-Conform stimulus has no explicit principle, we don't diagram. We articulate the moral of the story and look for the answer that matches it.

The tension: people complain about technology all the time, but when it comes down to it, they wouldn't give it up.

Slogan: *People gripe about technology, but they wouldn't live without it.*$pilot$), (2, $pilot$Goal$pilot$, $pilot$Look for a principle that says complaints about technology don't mean people would actually choose to go without it. The right answer should cover both halves: the complaints and the choice to keep the technology.$pilot$)) v(position,label,body) WHERE q.qid=$pilot$PT105-S4-Q12$pilot$ AND e.style='single' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lr_explanation_steps s WHERE s.explanation_id=e.id) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
